When teacher or student uploads an image through the Mini App:

Mini App
↓
multipart/form-data
↓
Python backend
↓
image temporarily held in memory or temporary file
↓
existing Gemini image analysis service
↓
structured result
↓
Firestore stores structured result
↓
temporary image deleted

Do NOT upload the image to:

* Firestore
* Firebase Storage
* S3
* Cloudinary
* permanent local storage

The image exists only long enough to perform Gemini analysis.

If a temporary file is used:

delete it in a `finally` block.

If reasonably possible, process the image from memory.

